A1. A Roman patriot and statesman. ~ CATO
A4. What a reformer makes us. ~ BORED
A8. Meaning "it won't be long now." ~ SOON
A11. Something bachelors steer clear of. ~ ALTAR
A12. What a bachelor might do to get to horizontal 11. ~ YIELD
A13. What Paul Revere did when he saw the light. ~ SPED
A15. The man who did this took a chance. ~ DICED
A17. The good old days. ~ YORE
A19. An obsolete measure of length. ~ ELL
A21. The pardner the Kaiser used to speak of. ~ GOD
A23. A slender stick. ~ ROD
A24. A street Arab. ~ GAMIN
A26. This is the end of any boat. ~ AFT
A27. One of those crossword animals. ~ GNU
A29. What kind of sermon bores the most? ~ LONGEST
A30. What Adam did in the Garden. ~ ATE
A32. This has an uprising every now and then. ~ ETNA
A34. Withered; dried up. ~ SEARED
A36. This afflicts husbands at about 3 A. M.—when they're asked where they've been. ~ INCOHERENCE
A38. What a materialist deals in. ~ MATTER
A40. A matter of weight. ~ TARE
A42. A prying fellow. ~ SPY
A43. What the husband does in a rage when he loses the argument. ~ DEPARTS
A46. The way we feel the first of every month. ~ SAD
A47. The baby stopped crying when they did this to him. ~ FED
A48. These are harder to pass than second-hand Fords. ~ TESTS
A49. What the best corn comes from. ~ COB
A51. The teacher's preference. ~ PET
A52. There's a point to this. ~ PIN
A54. High hat for "soon." ~ ANON
A56. A stone man. ~ MASON
A58. This keeps coming in and going out, but it isn't money. ~ TIDE
A59. A word we are apt to receive the first of the month. ~ REMIT
A60. He thought up "The Thinker." ~ RODIN
A61. A covering for out-door men. ~ TENT
A62. What we'd rather do than horizontal 59. ~ DEFER
A63. The Barber College yell. ~ NEXT

D1. Lawyers are always arguing about this. ~ CASE
D2. A weighty matter in China. ~ TAEL
D3. Something you'll be, if you live long enough. ~ OLD
D4. The kind of man that ruled the early West. ~ BAD
D5. An argument about this started a famous trial in Tennessee. ~ ORIGIN
D6. What the bold boy did when the pretty girl went by. ~ EYED
D7. Part of the verb "to do." ~ DID
D8. What horizontal 42 must be. ~ SLY
D9. This is what your nose knows. ~ ODOR
D10. Most people seem to be in this. ~ NEED
D14. A horticultural word sometimes used in crook stories. ~ PLANT
D16. What the crowd does when Lindbergh arrives. ~ CONGREGATES
D18. This is the way. ~ ROUTE
D20. An underworld friend. ~ PAL
D22. When do college boys like to date the pretty girls? ~ OFTEN
D25. What Barney Oldfield did along the road to fame. ~ MOTORED
D26. What the pretty girl usually does after she says "No." ~ ASSENTS
D27. Dumb Dora thinks these come from Germany. ~ GERMS
D28. There is strength in this, they say. ~ UNITY
D30. Restricted districts. ~ AREAS
D31. How the bashful youth started for the door. ~ EDGED
D33. An underground worker. ~ ANT
D35. There are at least two of these in the show. (Sing.) ~ ACT
D37. Grants. ~ CEDES
D39. There's strings to this one. ~ APRON
D41. Only a fast one can be this. ~ RAPID
D44. Simply ripping again. (Past.) ~ RETORE
D45. There's a lot of rooters here. ~ STY
D49. This follows the horses. ~ CART
D50. Everybody gets their start by being this. ~ BORN
D51. This is always on top. ~ PATE
D52. A tree. ~ PINE
D53. This is sometimes found in a tree. ~ NEST
D55. Many a poor fish gets caught in this. ~ NET
D56. This is the half-way place. ~ MID
D57. A conjunction. ~ NOR
D58. This can be found in any fliver on a country lane. ~ TIN


